236	2026-01-06 06:49:25.361364+00	2026-01-06 08:01:45.81673+00	<p><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt; text-indent: -36pt; font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);">In mosses the second gametophytic stage is leafy stage. Consider the following statements about leafy stage.</span></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">I. Leafy stage is produced from the secondary protonema as a lateral bud.</span><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">II. They consist of upright, slender axes bearing spirally arranged leaves.</span><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">III. They are attached to the soil through multicellular rhizoids.</span><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">IV. This leafy stage bears the sex organ.</span><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;">Which of the statements given above are correct?</span><span style="font-family: &quot;Cambria Math&quot;; font-size: 12pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><br></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><br></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><br></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><br></p><p class="15" style="margin-left:36.0000pt;"><br></p>	11		CHECKBOX		4	f	f	t	4eb4a6d2-d67a-412a-98f1-beea4d566045	00:01:00	\N	22	\N	\N	\N		\N
